V8's snapshot, generated on an Intel Mac for an x64 target that is not a Mac.

v8/gni/snapshot_toolchain.gni picks the HOST toolchain to build mksnapshot
when host and target share a cpu and differ in operating system - "targeting
win/x64 on a linux/x64 host". mksnapshot then compiles every builtin V8
embeds in the binary, and in this V8 a snapshot build takes the CPU features
those builtins may use from CpuFeaturesFromCompiler(): the __SSE4_1__,
__AVX__ and other macros of the compiler that built mksnapshot itself. That
is right when the host toolchain was configured with the target's -march,
which a Linux host is (-msse3, below). A Mac host is not: clang's default
CPU for x86_64-apple-macos is penryn, so __SSE4_1__ is defined and every
target built on an Intel Mac carries builtins that need SSE4.1 while its
own code was compiled for SSE3.

On an Apple Silicon Mac the same build is a cross-compile through
clang_arm64_v8_x64, whose compiler defines no x86 feature macros at all, so
nothing showed. Found on the first Intel-Mac build of node, whose first
JavaScript statement reached Builtins_MathMin and a pextrd - #UD on a CPU
without SSE4.1, which is QEMU's default one.

The fix is the host half compiled at the baseline the targets already use,
and only when the host toolchain is the snapshot toolchain for another
operating system's x64 target.
diff --git a/build/config/compiler_cpu_abi.gn b/build/config/compiler_cpu_abi.gn
index ae62bab587..e4bc7d5e2a 100644
--- a/build/config/compiler_cpu_abi.gn
+++ b/build/config/compiler_cpu_abi.gn
@@ -45,6 +45,21 @@ if (is_chromeos_device && is_chromeos) {
   }
 }
 
+# The Mac x64 host toolchain is also V8's snapshot toolchain whenever the
+# target is x64 on another operating system (v8/gni/snapshot_toolchain.gni,
+# "host_cpu == current_cpu"), and mksnapshot takes the CPU features of the
+# builtins it embeds from THIS compiler's macros - __SSE4_1__ and the rest.
+# Clang's default CPU for x86_64-apple-macos is penryn, so on an Intel Mac
+# the target's builtins would require SSE4.1 where its own code asks for
+# SSE3. Compile the host half at the baseline the targets below use.
+if (is_mac && current_cpu == "x64" && target_cpu == "x64" &&
+    target_os != "mac" && target_os != "ios") {
+  cpu_abi_cflags += [
+    "-march=x86-64",
+    "-msse3",
+  ]
+}
+
 if ((is_posix && !is_apple) || is_fuchsia) {
   # simplicity we always explicitly set the architecture.
   if (current_cpu == "x64") {
